From e6c28fdfa783a9f5c2dbb1526246ec1d310b91de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:51:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sampling, chat: K2-Horizon: hold EOG from a tool-call opener
 until the section is closed and its inner tags balance

Extends the Kimi-opener guard (84d7611e9). With tools offered the chat handling passes the
native tag pairs (request field no_empty_reply_hold, listed once in the K2 block of
chat-diff-analyzer.cpp: tool_calls, tool_call, arg_key, arg_type, arg_value; json format
uses tool_call only). From a native <ifm|tool_calls> or a Kimi opener EOG is masked until
the native section closed AND every inner pair is balanced; a close without its opener
closes nothing. Hard cap k_hold_cap = 2048 generated tokens (p99 real opencode call ~1200
tokens x2), then EOG is released and a debug line is logged. Never masks the last
candidate; cloned/reset with the sampler.

Forced-opener harness (stalled turn's prompt + opener, guard state seeded, 40 samples,
temp 0.8, 2600 tokens): pre-guard 23/40 EOG immediately; Kimi-only guard 0/40 EOG but
14/40 Kimi call left as reasoning text; this change 36/40 complete native call, 4/40 Kimi
loops/garbage that run to the cap (0/40 EOG). Inner tags in native calls: 0 unclosed;
2/40 emitted an extra </ifm|tool_calls>. Regression on the final build (replay, ~24K ctx):
40 stream + 40 non-stream + 40 stream opencode-DB shape: 0 Kimi, 0 empty, 0 leak, 0 stuck.
Tests: the new cases (open arg_value in a closed section, balanced xml_typed, json format,
cap, stray closes, no-tools) fail 14 checks against the previous guard; ctest -L main 59/59
and -R split-balance pass.

